tests: collect garbage before the backup tpool size tests

`BackupTestCase.test_default_tpool_size` and `test_tpool_size`
(cinder/tests/unit/backup/test_backup.py) assert that eventlet's native
thread pool is empty, `tpool._threads == []`, before and after they
build a BackupManager. The base TestCase cleanup calls `tpool.killall()`
after every test, so the first assertion holds. The second one fails
whenever something starts the pool between the two.

The garbage collector does. The Ceph backup driver tests
(cinder/tests/unit/backup/drivers/test_backup_ceph.py) build os-brick
`RBDVolumeIOWrapper` objects and leave them to the garbage collector,
some with an `eventlet.tpool.Proxy` as their image. The wrapper is an
`io.RawIOBase` and closes itself on finalization: `close()` calls
`flush()`, `flush()` calls `self.rbd_image.require_not_closed()`
(os_brick/initiator/linuxrbd.py), and the proxy runs that through
`tpool.execute()`, which starts all 20 threads. When a collection of
that garbage falls into the BackupManager construction of one of the two
tests, the test fails with

    AssertionError: Lists differ: [] != [<Thread(tpool_thread_0, ...

"Second list contains 20 additional elements." It needs the Ceph tests
earlier on the same stestr worker and a collection at that exact point,
and stestr spreads tests over workers in per-process hash order, so it
is rare: `test-service-images (cinder, 2025.2)` hit it once, in run
36865504387 on 2026-10-01. The volume manager twins of the two tests are
skipped upstream for the same class of failure (`self.skipTest("Bug
1811663")` in cinder/tests/unit/volume/test_volume.py).

The patch makes both tests start with `gc.collect()` followed by
`tpool.killall()`. Every finalizer that can start the pool runs before
the first assertion, the pool is stopped again, and nothing collectable
with such a finalizer is left for the rest of the test. The assertions
themselves are unchanged. Fixing the leak at its source would mean
closing the wrappers at the eleven places test_backup_ceph.py builds one,
and would still leave the two tests exposed to the next leak.

Shown with the garbage collector disabled for the run and one forced
`gc.collect()` at the second BackupManager construction of
`test_default_tpool_size`, after the test_backup_ceph module ran in the
same process: without the patch the test fails at its second assertion
with the 20 threads above, with the patch the collection frees no
wrapper and both tests pass.

The patch changes test code only, so it changes nothing at runtime and
tests/container-images/verify_cinder.sh needs no assertion.
The 2025.2 twin is
patches/cinder/2025.2/0004-tests-collect-garbage-before-the-backup-tpool-size-tests.patch;
it differs in the index line and the hunk offsets. The numbers differ
because 2025.2 carries the NetApp fakes backport as 0003.
No 2026.2 twin: 29.0.0 carries upstream commit c07c49c586, which
replaced both tests.

Applies to cinder 28.0.0 (2026.1).

Upstream status: not yet proposed. On master, commit c07c49c586 ("Run
Cinder's Backup service in native threads") replaced both tests together
with the tpool use they check, so the fix has no upstream target beyond
the stable branches.

diff --git a/cinder/tests/unit/backup/test_backup.py b/cinder/tests/unit/backup/test_backup.py
index 5aa554971..910149f5a 100644
--- a/cinder/tests/unit/backup/test_backup.py
+++ b/cinder/tests/unit/backup/test_backup.py
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 """Tests for Backup code."""
 
 import copy
+import gc
 import os
 from unittest import mock
 import uuid
@@ -1992,6 +1993,11 @@ class BackupTestCase(BaseBackupTest):
     @test.testtools.skipIf(issues.TPOOL_KILLALL_ISSUE, 'tpool.killall bug')
     def test_default_tpool_size(self):
         """Test we can set custom tpool size."""
+        # A garbage-collected os-brick RBDVolumeIOWrapper flushes through its
+        # tpool.Proxy and starts the pool. Collect what earlier tests left
+        # behind now, so that no finalizer runs between the assertions.
+        gc.collect()
+        tpool.killall()
         tpool._nthreads = 20
         self.assertListEqual([], tpool._threads)
 
@@ -2003,6 +2009,11 @@ class BackupTestCase(BaseBackupTest):
     @test.testtools.skipIf(issues.TPOOL_KILLALL_ISSUE, 'tpool.killall bug')
     def test_tpool_size(self):
         """Test we can set custom tpool size."""
+        # A garbage-collected os-brick RBDVolumeIOWrapper flushes through its
+        # tpool.Proxy and starts the pool. Collect what earlier tests left
+        # behind now, so that no finalizer runs between the assertions.
+        gc.collect()
+        tpool.killall()
         self.assertNotEqual(100, tpool._nthreads)
         self.assertListEqual([], tpool._threads)
 
